      "text": "1863  FA founded; Cambridge Rules adopted\n  1871  FA Cup (first major knockout competition)\n  1888  Football League founded (12 clubs):\n        Accrington, Aston Villa, Blackburn Rovers,\n        Bolton Wanderers, Burnley, Derby County,\n        Everton, Notts County, Preston North End,\n        Stoke, West Bromwich Albion, Wolverhampton W.\n        -- Preston: unbeaten season 1888-89\n        -- First professional players officially recognized\n  1895  Crystal Palace becomes first FA Cup final venue\n  1904  FIFA founded (Paris, 7 founding nations)\n  1930  First FIFA World Cup (Montevideo, Uruguay)\n        Uruguay won (home nation, summer in Southern\n        Hemisphere -- no European nations attended except\n        Romania, Yugoslavia, France, Belgium)\n  1950  World Cup Brazil (Maracanazo: Uruguay beats\n        Brazil 2-1 in front of 200,000 at Maracana,\n        effectively largest crowd ever at a football match)\n  1954  West Germany beats Hungary 3-2 (Miracle of Bern)\n        -- Reconstructed nation's first major triumph\n  1966  England host and win (Geoff Hurst hat-trick,\n        4-2 vs West Germany, Wembley)\n  1970  Brazil's third World Cup (Pele's last) -- best\n        ever Brazil team (some argue best ever team)\n  1986  Maradona's World Cup: Hand of God + Goal of\n        Century vs England (Argentina won tournament)\n  1992  Premier League formed: breakaway from Football\n        League; Sky Sports deal transforms revenue\n  1992  UEFA Champions League (rebranding of European Cup)\n  1994  USA hosts World Cup; US Soccer infrastructure\n        expands; MLS formed 1996\n  2000s Real Madrid \"Galacticos\" model: Zidane, Beckham,\n        Ronaldo R9, Figo -- marketing-first recruitment\n  2009  Ronaldo to Real Madrid: £80M world record\n  2022  Qatar World Cup: Messi wins his only World Cup\n        (Argentina beat France on penalties)\n```"
    },
