      "text": "1892  William Heffelfinger paid $500 for one game\n        (first professional payment documented)\n  1895  Professional league attempts begin and fail\n  1920  American Professional Football Association founded\n        (Canton, Ohio; Jim Thorpe elected president)\n  1922  Renamed: National Football League (NFL)\n  1936  NFL draft introduced (equalizes talent distribution)\n  1950s Paul Brown (Cleveland Browns) innovations:\n        film study, playbook system, intelligence testing,\n        face mask (Groza's suggestion), messenger guards\n  1958  NFL Championship \"Greatest Game Ever Played\"\n        Baltimore Colts vs New York Giants, OT\n        TV audience: 45M -- transforms public perception\n  1960  American Football League founded (AFL):\n        competition for players, new franchises, new cities\n  1966  AFL-NFL merger agreement\n  1967  Super Bowl I: Green Bay Packers 35-10 KC Chiefs\n        (Lombardi's Packers, Bart Starr)\n  1970  AFL-NFL merger complete; Monday Night Football\n  1978  16-game season; passing rule liberalization\n        (defenders can't jam receivers beyond 5 yards)\n        -- The \"Mel Blount Rule\" -- transforms passing game\n  1982  Players strike (57 days, shortened season)\n  1993  Salary cap introduced ($34.6M per team initially)\n  1994  Two-point conversion adopted\n  2011  CBA: rookie wage scale, expanded season debate\n```"
